# Buttons

Every clickable action is a box: the shared `Button` (or `buttonClassName` on a router `Link`) from `shared-components/Button.tsx`. A bare word like "change name" or "delete" reads as a link, so it never stands alone as an action. This is every screen, including ones already shipped.

`Button` draws a 1px border and a fill, and a hover that changes a colour or the border: no shadow, no press movement (no-box-shadow.mdc).

- **A commit** (make it, go live, log in, the yes on a dialog): `variant="primary"`, the default size.
- **A small action in a row** (rename, add, kick, save, cancel, the no on a confirm): `size="sm"`. It is `px-3 py-1.5 text-sm`, a `primaryStroke` border that hovers to a lifted fill and a stronger stroke, a `primaryBlue` focus outline, `opacity-50` and no hover when disabled, and `max-md:min-h-11` so it stays a thumb's height on a phone. Pick the variant:
  - `variant="secondary"` (default): a neutral action.
  - `variant="outline"`: the one action in the row that moves things forward (add, save, join).
  - `variant="outline-danger"`: delete, remove, kick, leave, ban. Destructive is always outline danger, never a bare red word.
- **A row too tight for words**: an icon-only button, with an `aria-label` and a `Tooltip` of the same name (tooltips.mdc).
- **A plain inline link** only inside a sentence ("no account? <u>sign up</u>"), where it is part of what the sentence says. A word sitting alone beside a field or at the end of a row is not in a sentence: box it.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — bare words that read as links, and a one-off box
<button type="button" className="text-sm text-textSecondary hover:underline">change name</button>
<button type="button" className="text-sm text-textTertiary">delete</button>
<button className="border px-3 py-1.5 text-sm">add role</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<Button size="sm" onClick={rename}>change name</Button>
<Button size="sm" variant="outline" type="submit" disabled={!ok}>add role</Button>
<Button size="sm" variant="outline-danger" onClick={remove}>delete</Button>

// ✅ GOOD — a tight row
<Tooltip content="remove">
  <button type="button" aria-label="remove" onClick={remove}><RiCloseLine aria-hidden size={16} /></button>
</Tooltip>

// ✅ GOOD — a link inside a sentence
<p>no account? <button type="button" className="text-primaryBlue hover:underline" onClick={toSignup}>sign up</button></p>
```

Do not invent a one-off bordered chip for a new control: reach for `Button` and a `size`/`variant`. A pressed or selected state is colour (`border-primaryBlue text-primaryBlue`), not a new outline.
